**Short Story:**  
In the shadowy depths of Stranglethorn Vale, a Gnome Warlock named Thalric trudged through the undergrowth, his succubus companion, Zynvara, perched on his shoulder. Zynvara, with her crimson eyes and sly grin, was in her element, her tail flicking as she scouted ahead. "Careful, little one," Thalric muttered, adjusting the straps of his bag. "We’re not here for trouble."  

Zynvara chuckled, her voice a sultry whisper. "Oh, Thalric, trouble is half the fun."  

As they ventured deeper, a group of bandits ambushed them, their weapons glinting in the dim light. Thalric froze, his heart pounding, but Zynvara was ready. With a flick of her tail, she unleashed a cloud of enchantments, disorienting the attackers. Thalric seized the moment, channeling his void magic to blast the bandits back.  

Exhausted but victorious, Thalric knelt to thank Zynvara. "You really are the best," he said, stroking her fur.  

Zynvara purred, her eyes glinting mischievously. "Of course, my dear. After all, I’m your *favorite* companion."  

---

**Answer:**  
The reason most warlocks are seen with voidwalkers, despite succubuses being better for leveling and questing, is because succubuses have a skill called *Charm*, which increases the chance of attracting wandering monsters. This makes them more commonly seen in combat situations, even though their questing abilities are superior.
</answer> [end of text]


